keycloak setup

lowForge K8s OIDC Authentication Guide
This system uses Keycloak 26 to provide Identity-based access to the Kubernetes cluster.

Phase 1: Keycloak Infrastructure (Server Side)
We deployed Keycloak on Kubernetes using NFS for data persistence.

Storage Strategy: Used a Static PV/PVC pointing to 10.0.1.27:/var/nfs/flowforge/keycloak.
Deployment Strategy: Used strategy: type: Recreate to prevent H2 database file locks during updates.
Key Configuration:
KC_PROXY_HEADERS: xforwarded (For SSL Support)
KC_HOSTNAME: https://keycloak.flowforge.fun
KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN: Setup the master admin credentials.
Phase 2: Keycloak Configuration (Identity Side)
These steps were performed in the Keycloak UI:

Create Realm: Name: flowforge.
Create Client:
ID: kubernetes
Client Authentication: ON
Valid Redirect URIs: http://localhost:8000/* and http://localhost:18000/*
Create Groups Mapper:
Go to Client kubernetes -> Client Scopes -> dedicated -> Add Mapper.
Type: Group Membership.
Name/Token Claim: groups.
Create Groups & Users:
Groups created: cluster-admins, dev-team, test-team.
Users created and assigned to their respective groups.
Phase 3: Cluster Integration (Master Node)
The Kubernetes API server was configured to trust Keycloak as an identity provider.

1. Run this Python script on the Master Node:

python
import yaml
path = '/etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml'
with open(path, 'r') as f:
    config = yaml.safe_load(f)
flags = [
    '--oidc-issuer-url=https://keycloak.flowforge.fun/realms/flowforge',
    '--oidc-client-id=kubernetes',
    '--oidc-username-claim=email',
    '--oidc-groups-claim=groups',
    '--oidc-groups-prefix=oidc:',
]
cmds = config['spec']['containers'][0]['command']
cmds = [c for c in cmds if not c.startswith('--oidc-')]
cmds.extend(flags)
config['spec']['containers'][0]['command'] = cmds
with open(path, 'w') as f:
    yaml.dump(config, f)
