Headlamp OIDC Integration Guide
1. HAProxy Configuration (Load Balancer)
We updated the load balancer to handle two things:

Routing: Added headlamp.flowforge.fun to the ACLs.
Buffer Size: Increased tune.bufsize to 32768.
Why? OIDC tokens and cookies are very large. Without this, HAProxy would cut the connection, causing ERR_HTTP2_PROTOCOL_ERROR.
2. Keycloak Setup (Identity Provider)
We created a new client named headlamp:

Client Authentication: Enabled (Confidential).
Valid Redirect URIs: https://headlamp.flowforge.fun/oidc-callback.
Audience Mapper: Added a mapper to include kubernetes in the token audience (aud).
Why? The Kubernetes API server will reject any token that doesn't explicitly list kubernetes as its intended audience.
3. Kubernetes Routing (Gateway API)
We created a new HTTPRoute for Headlamp:

Hostname: headlamp.flowforge.fun.
Backend: Pointed to the headlamp service on port 80.
ParentRef: Attached to the dashboard-gateway.
4. Headlamp Deployment (OIDC Flags)
We patched the Headlamp deployment with these arguments:

-in-cluster: Allows Headlamp to talk to the API server internally.
-oidc-idp-issuer-url: Points to the Keycloak realm.
-oidc-client-id & -oidc-client-secret: The credentials for the headlamp client.
-oidc-callback-url: Must match Keycloak exactly.
-oidc-skip-tls-verify: Required because Headlamp runs inside the cluster and needs to trust the external Keycloak URL.
-oidc-use-pkce: Enabled for modern security standards.
5. RBAC & Visibility
We added a specific ClusterRole called flowforge-namespace-lister.

What it does: Allows the dev-team and test-team to list the names of all namespaces.
Why? Headlamp's UI requires this permission to populate the namespace dropdown menu. Without it, the dashboard appears empty for restricted users.
Security: It only allows seeing the names. Users still cannot see pods or secrets inside namespaces they don't own (like kube-system).
Final User Experience:
User visits https://headlamp.flowforge.fun.
Clicks "Sign in with OIDC".
Logs in via Keycloak.
Redirected back to Headlamp.
Admins: See everything.
Teams: See the namespace list, click "dev", and manage their specific resources._ |
