wiping data

1. Scale the StatefulSet to 0
This forces the Postgres pod to shut down and detach from the volume.

delete the pvc

bash
kubectl scale statefulset postgres -n dev --replicas=0
2. Wait for the pod to disappear
bash
kubectl get pods -n dev | grep postgres
(Wait until no postgres pod is listed).

5. Delete the StatefulSet to trigger recreation
Now that the volume is totally gone, delete the scaled-down StatefulSet so Argo CD can deploy a fresh one with a brand new, empty volume:

bash
kubectl delete statefulset postgres -n dev
Wait about 30 seconds for Argo CD to recreate the pod. Once kubectl get pods -n dev shows postgres-0 is 1/1 Running, you can run your final restart:

bash
kubectl rollout restart deployment -n dev

